  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme of evaluation in industry - strengthening of the three current centers and creation of two new ones in Colombian universities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project &quot;Programme of evaluation in industry - strengthening of the three current centers and creation of two new ones in Colombian universities&quot; (hereinafter simply PEVI project) aims to enhance energy efficiency of Colombia industry through the establishment of a network of industrial assessment centres tasked to carry out energy assessments/audits of/in small- and medium-sized enterprises (SME) and to strengthen existing and future workforce for industrial energy efficiency and decarbonization. The PEVI project would build on and reinforce results achieved through past UNIDO-UPME joint activities by working with three existing PEVI centres and supporting establishment of two new ones.  The PEVI project, through 5 centres, would carry out 40 energy audits and train more than 150 industrial energy efficiency practitioners. The PEVI project would work  on evaluating impact of past energy audits#, designate one of the PEVI Centres as  network lead for better coordination, and fostering collaboration across industrial sectors. Moreover, the PEVI project seeks to develop a sustainability strategy to secure long-term funding and ensuring continued growth and effectiveness of the PEVI centres in promoting energy efficiency and green jobs in Colombia.</narrative>
  </description>
